# Temporary debug sideload APKs (RUNBOOK §7) — never committed. Send the build to the owner via the
# file tool, or grab the build.yml `app-debug` CI artifact. `clean-dist.yml` is a backstop for a forced add.
/dist/

# Tasker source project — kept out of the tree (1.6 MB); owner picks LFS-vs-ignore at PR review (S12.9a).
# Reference recipes live in docs/rebuild/XML_RECIPES.md.
docs/rebuild/extraction/_source/Advanced_Auto_Brightness_V3.3.prj_9.xml

# Credentials — file-kind cover for the value-shape scan in scripts/guards/staged-secrets.sh.
# That guard reads staged blobs for secret SHAPES; these rules keep whole credential FILES from
# being staged at all. The two are complementary: neither subsumes the other.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
signing.properties
*.p12
*.pepk
google-services.json
.env
# Deliberately un-negated: `.env.*` also covers a `.env.example`, and nothing here needs one.
# A committed template would be a file that LOOKS ignored while being tracked, in the one
# directory where that misreading is expensive. If a real need appears, force-add it explicitly.
.env.*
secrets.properties
